{"name":"Ancient Ruins","hex":"#e0cac0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ancient","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having lasted from a remote period; having been of long duration; of great age, very old.","Existent or occurring in time long past, usually in remote ages; belonging to or associated with antiquity; old, as opposed to modern."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is very old.","A person who lived in ancient times."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancient"},{"term":"ruins","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of ruin"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of ruin"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruins"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ruins","blocks":[{"text":"Ruins are the remains of a civilization's architecture. The term refers to formerly intact structures that have fallen into a state of partial or total disrepair over time due to a variety of factors, such as lack of maintenance, deliberate destruction by humans, or uncontrollable destruction by natural phenomena. The most common root causes that yield ruins in their wake are natural disasters, armed conflict, and population decline, with many structures becoming progressively derelict over time due to long-term weathering and scavenging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Gymnasion_und_Therme_aus_S%C3%BCdwest.jpg/330px-Gymnasion_und_Therme_aus_S%C3%BCdwest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruins","wikidata":"Q109607"},{"title":"Ancient history","blocks":[{"text":"Ancient history is a time period from the beginning of writing and recorded human history through late antiquity. The span of recorded history is roughly 5,000 years, beginning with the development of Sumerian cuneiform script. Ancient history covers all continents inhabited by humans in the period 3000 BC – AD 500."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Denis_Bourez_-_British_Museum%2C_London_%288747049029%29_%282%29.jpg/330px-Denis_Bourez_-_British_Museum%2C_London_%288747049029%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_history","wikidata":"Q41493"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg/500px-Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg/500px-Surb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Holy Saviour's Church in Gyumri after the 1988 Armenian earthquake, the strongest earthquake in the USSR in terms of the number of victims","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASurb_Amenaprkitch.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg/500px-Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg/1280px-Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg/500px-Post-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1906 San Francisco earthquake: Ruins in vicinity of Post and Grant Avenue.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APost-and-Grant-Avenue-Look.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Whitby_Abbey_060615.jpg/500px-Whitby_Abbey_060615.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c